# Loose API-key drops at the repo root (Dockerfile.app does `COPY . .`,
# so an unignored key file gets baked into the published image).
# These are deliberately BROAD: on 2026-09-15 a key was dropped as
# `sam-gov-key.txt`, which matched none of the original `*_api_key*` patterns
# because it used hyphens and omitted the word "api". Match on "key" anywhere
# in the name rather than trying to predict the spelling.
*_api_key.txt
*_api_key
fathom_api_key.txt
*api_key*
*api-key*
*_key.txt
*-key.txt
*_key
*-key
*.key
*.pem
key.txt

# Local data drops (exported Google Sheets, scratch extracts). Dockerfile.app
# ends in `COPY . .`, so an unignored CSV at the repo root is both committed
# and baked into the published image.
*.csv
local-data/

# Same vocabulary problem as the key patterns above: an OAuth credential is
# spelled with neither "key" nor "api", so OAUTH_CLIENT_ID.txt matched nothing.
# These are already in .gcloudignore; mirrored here so the file is not
# committable either.
*oauth*
*OAUTH*
*client_id*
*CLIENT_ID*
*client-id*
*secret*
*SECRET*

# BW&CO playbooks, the NIH knowledge base, and the client strategy packets
# they produced (named clients: assessments, pursue orders, IC scoring).
# Dockerfile.app ends in `COPY . .`, so committing this folder would publish
# client-confidential material into the matcher-app image in Artifact Registry.
# The playbooks and knowledge base live in GCS under strategy-playbooks/ —
# see src/modules/strategy_session.py.
project-context/
